==Bulgarian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|bg|старъ}} {{bg-PRO}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|bg|sla-pro|*starъ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{bg-IPA}}

===Adjective===
{{bg-adj|стар|absn=ста́рост}}

# [[old]] {{gloss|having lived or existed for a relatively long period of time}}
#: {{syn|bg|възрастен}}
# [[out of date]], [[obsolete]], [[outdated]], [[old-fashioned]]
#: {{syn|bg|отживял|старомоден}}
# [[worn out]] {{gloss|damaged and useless due to hard or continued use}}
#: {{syn|bg|извехтял|износен}}
# [[hand-me-down]]
# [[former]], [[previous]]
#: {{syn|bg|бивш|предишен}}

====Usage notes====
This term is seldom used comparatively (i.e. {{m|bg|по́-стар}}) in reference to humans, as it typically bears connotations of especially old age. Largely, {{m|bg|голя́м}} is favoured over {{lang|bg|стар}} when comparing ages, whereas the latter is used when simply declaring the age of an elderly person.

